      {
        "id": 184580,
        "name": "jorgenp",
        "username": "jorgenp",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/958977/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2016-11-20T01:59:04.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>OK, new thoughts on your log, Jeysie:</p><ul>\n<li>You've shown that redirection either requires reduction/immunity, or that the only redirection that counts is Abject Refugees itself.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>It seems that damage initiated against Captain Cosmic and redirected elsewhere does count towards the total of 20, despite the damage reduced by Energy Bracers attached to Captain Cosmic not seeming to count.&nbsp; Alchemical Redirection was a useful card to have in these tests.</li>\n</ul><p>Given these, the unlock condition might be something along the lines of:</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Prime Wardens Argent Adet must be unlocked.&nbsp; Then in the Dok'Thortah Capital with Captain Cosmic, the total of damage redirected from Abject Refugees to Captain Cosmic and damage reduced by Captain Cosmic's Energy Bracers to other Heroes must be at least 20.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I suppose I still haven't figured out what's up with the Wounding Buffer delay to the unlock, though...&nbsp; Perhaps it's just a weird quirk in the timing?</p>",
        "post_number": 130,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:09:57.518Z",
